    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Sequence of tenses",
     "texto": [
      "After an introductory verb in the past, the present usually becomes the imperfect, the passé composé becomes the plus-que-parfait and the future becomes the conditional: **Il dit : «Je viendrai»** → **Il a dit qu'il viendrait**. If the fact is still true or current, the present can also be kept."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Keeping the time relation",
     "texto": [
      "An earlier action becomes plus-que-parfait: **«J'ai terminé»** → **Elle a dit qu'elle avait terminé**. A later action becomes conditional: **«Je partirai»** → **Elle a dit qu'elle partirait**. It does not change the meaning of the message; it changes the point of reference."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
